<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Continuous Integration on KevCaz's Website</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/tags/continuous-integration/</link><description>Recent content in Continuous Integration on KevCaz's Website</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><copyright>Content under CC0 1.0 Universal unless otherwise specified.</copyright><lastBuildDate>Sun, 12 Apr 2020 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://kevcaz.github.io/tags/continuous-integration/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Deploy a pkgdown website on gh-pages manually</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2020/04/2020-04-12_deploy_a_pkgdown/</link><pubDate>Sun, 12 Apr 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2020/04/2020-04-12_deploy_a_pkgdown/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This is another note about deploying a
&lt;a href="https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=pkgdown"&gt;&lt;code&gt;pkgdown&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;sup id="fnref:1"&gt;&lt;a href="#fn:1" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref"&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; website with
&lt;a href="https://travis-ci.org/"&gt;Travis&lt;/a&gt; on gh-pages. I had
&lt;a href="notes/ci/deploypkgdown"&gt;previously&lt;/a&gt; used the package
&lt;a href="https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=travis"&gt;&lt;code&gt;travis&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; but I was recently
interested in doing so manually. Fortunately, I found this very helpful
&lt;a href="https://gist.github.com/gaborcsardi/68960fb01bec74d89611bb9c2b0b7e5a"&gt;walk-through&lt;/a&gt;
by &lt;a href="https://github.com/gaborcsardi"&gt;Gábor Csárdi&lt;/a&gt;&lt;sup id="fnref:2"&gt;&lt;a href="#fn:2" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref"&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;. I used it and it worked
well for a while, but at some point I had an issue with the deployment part
(still not sure why), so I changed it. Instead of using the following
config&lt;sup id="fnref:3"&gt;&lt;a href="#fn:3" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref"&gt;3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;
&lt;table style="border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-yaml" data-lang="yaml"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;deploy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;provider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ea9d34"&gt;script&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;script&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ea9d34"&gt;Rscript -e &amp;#39;pkgdown::deploy_site_github()&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;skip_cleanup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#286983"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;all_branches&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#286983"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;I now use&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Generate a ssh key with R</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2020/04/2020-04-04_generate_a_ssh/</link><pubDate>Sat, 04 Apr 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2020/04/2020-04-04_generate_a_ssh/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I now frequently use &lt;a href="https://github.com/features/actions"&gt;GitHub actions&lt;/a&gt; to
deploy websites on gh-pages. One way to do so requires to use a &lt;a href="https://help.github.com/en/github/authenticating-to-github/generating-a-new-ssh-key-and-adding-it-to-the-ssh-agent#generating-a-new-ssh-key"&gt;ssh
key&lt;/a&gt;
(the full procedure is well explained, &lt;em&gt;inter alia&lt;/em&gt;, in the README of
&lt;a href="https://github.com/peaceiris/actions-gh-pages"&gt;peaceiris/actions-gh-pages&lt;/a&gt;). As
I am used to work with the Terminal, when I need such a key, I use the following
command line:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;
&lt;table style="border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;$ ssh-keygen -t rsa -b &lt;span style="color:#ea9d34"&gt;4096&lt;/span&gt; -C &lt;span style="color:#ea9d34"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#286983"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;git config user.email&lt;span style="color:#286983"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ea9d34"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; -f gh-pages -N &lt;span style="color:#ea9d34"&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;which generates two files:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>GitHub actions, checkout and submodule</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2019/12/2019-12-04_github_actions_checkout/</link><pubDate>Wed, 04 Dec 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2019/12/2019-12-04_github_actions_checkout/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I now use &lt;a href="https://github.com/features/actions"&gt;GitHub Actions&lt;/a&gt; to deploy this website (see my &lt;a href="../githubactions"&gt;previous note about it&lt;/a&gt;) and last Monday (two days ago &amp;#x1f603;) after I pushed I got an email saying the deployment failed and found the following error message in the console log:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;
&lt;table style="border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#9893a5"&gt;##[error]The input &amp;#39;submodules&amp;#39; is not supported in actions/checkout@v2&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Turns out this is because version 2 of &lt;a href="https://github.com/actions/checkout"&gt;checkout&lt;/a&gt; does not support submodule yet (see this issue report &lt;a href="https://github.com/actions/checkout/issues/81"&gt;https://github.com/actions/checkout/issues/81&lt;/a&gt;) which I use to install my &lt;a href="https://github.com/KevCaz/hugo-KevCaz"&gt;Hugo Theme&lt;/a&gt;. All I had to do was to use a previous version, so I replaced &lt;code&gt;uses: actions/checkout@master&lt;/code&gt; by &lt;code&gt;uses: actions/checkout@v1.2.0&lt;/code&gt; in my &lt;a href="https://github.com/KevCaz/KevCaz.github.io"&gt;&lt;code&gt;deploy.yaml&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; file:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>My first workflow with GitHub Actions</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2019/11/2019-11-20_my_first_workflow/</link><pubDate>Wed, 20 Nov 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2019/11/2019-11-20_my_first_workflow/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;As explained on &lt;a href="https://github.com/features/actions"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitHub Actions makes it easy to automate all your software workflows, now with world-class CI/CD. Build, test, and deploy your code right from GitHub. Make code reviews, branch management, and issue triaging work the way you want.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve heard about this feature and I decided to give it a first go yesterday as I
wanted to deploy a notebook for the &lt;a href="https://github.com/McCannLab/TheoryClub"&gt;McCann Lab&amp;rsquo;s Theory
Club&lt;/a&gt; built with
&lt;a href="https://bookdown.org/"&gt;bookdown&lt;/a&gt;. As it uses the form of an R package, I figured
the easiest approach was to google &amp;ldquo;github actions R&amp;rdquo; and this is how I learned
about the R package &lt;a href="https://github.com/r-lib/ghactions"&gt;ghactions&lt;/a&gt;. This
package generates the file you need to set up your GitHub Actions workflow, i.e.
a &lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YAML"&gt;YAML file&lt;/a&gt; in &lt;code&gt;.github/workflows&lt;/code&gt;. Given
that the notebook I was deploying was a static website I opted for &lt;code&gt;website()&lt;/code&gt;
as a workflow:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Deploy a pkgdown on gh-pages</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2019/10/2019-10-22_deploy_a_pkgdown/</link><pubDate>Tue, 22 Oct 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2019/10/2019-10-22_deploy_a_pkgdown/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;There are three ways to &lt;a href="https://help.github.com/en/github/working-with-github-pages/configuring-a-publishing-source-for-your-github-pages-site"&gt;deploy a website on your GitHub pages&lt;/a&gt; :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;using the &lt;code&gt;gh-pages&lt;/code&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;using the folder &lt;code&gt;docs&lt;/code&gt; on your master branch;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;using the master branch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I frequently use the GitHub pages to deploy the &lt;a href="https://github.com/r-lib/pkgdown"&gt;pkgdown&lt;/a&gt; websites I create for my R packages. For a while, I was using the &lt;code&gt;docs/&lt;/code&gt; folder where the website is generated by default. But I figured that this way has two main drawbacks:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I needed to rebuild the package locally after (pretty much) any change in the package;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;it adds a huge amount of changes in the commit history.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That&amp;rsquo;s why I&amp;rsquo;ve decided to make &lt;a href="https://travis-ci.org/"&gt;Travis&lt;/a&gt; build the
website and deploy it on the &lt;code&gt;gh-branch&lt;/code&gt; (many developers smartly use this
approach which actually is the default branch for Travis). After tweaking
&lt;code&gt;travis.yml&lt;/code&gt; (see &lt;a href="https://docs.travis-ci.com/user/deployment/pages/"&gt;Travis documentation about this&lt;/a&gt;) I ran into two problems.
First, I needed a deploy key:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Reasonably complex matrix build with Travis</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2019/07/2019-07-02_reasonably_complex_matrix/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Jul 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2019/07/2019-07-02_reasonably_complex_matrix/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.travis-ci.com/user/build-matrix/"&gt;Matrix build&lt;/a&gt; is a very powerful feature of &lt;a href="https://travis-ci.com/"&gt;Travis CI&lt;/a&gt;: it allows you to
define a list of custom environments wherein your software will be built. For instead, I check &lt;a href="https://travis-ci.org/ropensci/rcites"&gt;rcites on 4 different environments&lt;/a&gt; (note that Travis offers 3 different Ubuntu version, &lt;a href="https://docs.travis-ci.com/user/reference/osx/"&gt;several MacOSX images&lt;/a&gt; and that the support for &lt;a href="https://docs.travis-ci.com/user/reference/windows/"&gt;Windows is in early stage&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A few days ago, the matrix build I used for another R &amp;#x1f4e6; failed with the following error (see &lt;a href="https://travis-ci.com/mangal-wg/rmangal/jobs/211574578"&gt;https://travis-ci.com/mangal-wg/rmangal/jobs/211574578&lt;/a&gt; for the log):&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sent your R package to package builder via devtools</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2019/05/2019-05-23_sent_your_r/</link><pubDate>Thu, 23 May 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2019/05/2019-05-23_sent_your_r/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;As I was sending a minor patch to &lt;a href="https://github.com/ropensci/rcites"&gt;rcites&lt;/a&gt;,
I use &lt;code&gt;devtools::build_win()&lt;/code&gt; and got the following warning message:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Warning message:
&amp;#39;devtools::build_win&amp;#39; is deprecated.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;And the message suggested to check out &lt;code&gt;check_win_*&lt;/code&gt;, and I so did a quick
check:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;
&lt;table style="border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-R" data-lang="R"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;R&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;devtools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;check&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;once &lt;code&gt;tab&lt;/code&gt; typed, the following function names were prompted:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;
&lt;table style="border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f"&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#575279;background-color:#faf4ed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-R" data-lang="R"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;devtools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;check_built&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;devtools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;check_cran&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;devtools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;check_win_oldrelease&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;devtools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;check_man&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;devtools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;check&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;devtools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;check_win_release&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;devtools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;check_win_devel&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;devtools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;check_dep_version&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;devtools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;check_failures&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;devtools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#797593"&gt;::&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#d7827e"&gt;check_rhub&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We now have access to &lt;a href="https://builder.r-hub.io/"&gt;rhub&lt;/a&gt; via
&lt;a href="https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/devtools/index.html"&gt;devtools&lt;/a&gt;, that&amp;rsquo;s
neat &amp;#x1f386;! I knew it&amp;rsquo;d happen at some point, but did not know it was
already available!, everything is going very fast, am I the only one struggling
to keep up?&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Run your jobs one by one on Travis!</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2018/11/2018-11-19_run_your_jobs/</link><pubDate>Mon, 19 Nov 2018 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2018/11/2018-11-19_run_your_jobs/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I now test &lt;a href="https://github.com/ropensci/rcites"&gt;rcites&lt;/a&gt; for &lt;a href="https://travis-ci.org/ropensci/rcites"&gt;4 configurations
on Travis&lt;/a&gt; so Travis runs 4 jobs. For a
while, I was running all the jobs at once, and as rcites is R-client for a
web API, many of the jobs failed because of the well-known error 429:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Too Many Requests (RFC 6585) (HTTP 429).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I always ended restarting some jobs, I coped with it. At some point, I stepped
back and thought: &amp;ldquo;people people behind Travis are smart,
so they should have thought about limiting concurrent jobs&amp;rdquo;. You bet they did!
It&amp;rsquo;s one of the many settings available. So I simply switched the button
&lt;code&gt;Limit concurrent jobs&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;Settings/General&lt;/code&gt; and on a set the limit to 1.
No more HTTP 429!&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>rcites code coverage dropped to 0</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2018/10/2018-10-09_rcites_code_coverage/</link><pubDate>Tue, 09 Oct 2018 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2018/10/2018-10-09_rcites_code_coverage/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;We (a couple of colleagues and myself) are currently finishing a major release
for our R package &lt;a href="https://github.com/ibartomeus/rcites"&gt;rcites&lt;/a&gt;. After adding the latest
feature I have been working on via a pull request, I messed up with my local
master branch and overwrite/delete some files &amp;#x1f620;. I thought it was not
a big deal as all of them were files created/edited when the package is built (well, I
thought so). But after the very next push, &lt;a href="https://github.com/ibartomeus/rcites/issues/37"&gt;the code coverage weirdly dropped to
zero&lt;/a&gt; &amp;#x1f631;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Let AppVeyor watch inSileco!</title><link>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2018/10/2018-10-02_let_appveyor_watch/</link><pubDate>Tue, 02 Oct 2018 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://kevcaz.github.io/notes/2018/10/2018-10-02_let_appveyor_watch/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I very much enjoy sharing thoughts and code on our blog &lt;a href="https://insileco.github.io/"&gt;inSileco&lt;/a&gt;. Recently, one of the authors
mentioned that &lt;a href="https://github.com/inSileco/inSileco.github.io/issues/62"&gt;he was not able to clone the repository&lt;/a&gt;
on his Windows machine. I came to realize that we better not assume that everybody is working on MacOS or Linux and check that inSileco works well on Windows. One of the most convenient way to do so is to use &lt;a href="https://www.appveyor.com/"&gt;AppVeyor&lt;/a&gt; and I
therefore decided to spend some time making the &lt;a href="https://ci.appveyor.com/project/KevCaz/insileco-github-io"&gt;build passed on AppVeyor&lt;/a&gt;!&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>